      "addedAt": "2026-11-27T03:56:33.054Z",
      "text": "The 'this host is not connected' flake from #510/#518: agents.rs a_hub_hands_the_agents_it_kept_to_their_host_once_and_safely failed 1/6 in the whole agents binary under 8 CPU burners (RUST_TEST_THREADS=8) at #518's head, at the ask right after the hand-over (agents.rs:656). That message comes only from remote::Pipe::send with the pipe not open (up=false). Its kept sandboxes (/tmp/yardd-test-1015910-agents-migrate-{hub-15,remote-12}) show the test's client connected to the hub before the hand-over finished; the remote logged 5 connections (the test's, the hub's monitor, the adopt and settled requests, each its own socket in remote::request, and the window's pipe), so the pipe did open, but the log has no times to say when. The deterministic test (proof 4) shows the same state on demand: the hub shows the host connected while a page's own pipe is still opening, and the page's op is refused."
    },
